<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The spacer enclave (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release C"; DESIGN.md "Rimfolk's peoples"; Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/):
    high-tech brokers who live on the planet between its towns and the ships above, buying from the one and selling to
    the other. Spacer, on the game's outlander parent: coats of every cut dyed pale cyan, marshals in one issue of recon
    armour and a charge weapon, a few bionics, a few psylinks (their kinds, below). Very few towns (settlementGenerationWeight 0.3), each a market round a landing pad
    (TownPlanDef Rimfolk_Plan_LandingMarket). Their caravans walk with pack beasts as the Empire's do, less often than
    another people's (caravanWeight 0.7); for an industrial or spacer colony their factor asks by radio for leave to come
    down by the gate with goods, and comes by drop pod when bidden (Rimfolk_Evt_EnclaveLander). Busy orbital lanes and a
    ship come down come from them likeliest (Patches/Rimfolk_PeoplesC.xml). Their factor offers salvage from above for a
    share of its worth, dropped by pod at the colony's trade spot (Rimfolk_Evt_EnclaveSalvage), in every age. Their
    founding (the description): Ines Okoro, purser of a downed ore hauler, who sold its cargo, passage and debts one
    bargain at a time; the hauler's manifest. What they honour, fear and say is in their template (on their card). They
    defend their markets and raid only when
    the colony has turned them hostile (raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve 0.15: few, and well armed). Listed once among the
    world's peoples when a world is made, never required. Faith (Ideology): a fixed creed of the body improved (VE Memes'
    trader and progressive where loaded), the techist style. Kind of people (Biotech): seven in ten baseliners; hussars, genies,
    highmates, Odyssey's starjacks, Vanilla Races Expanded's archons and androids, the Avaloi, Alpha Genes' lapis, and
    Rimsenal's Åskbarns and Uredde, the made soldiers of an old spacer project.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Enclave</defName>
    <label>spacer enclave</label>
    <description>An enclave of brokers who live between the planet's towns and the ships above it, buying from the one and selling to the other. They keep a few markets round their landing pads and come down by drop pod wherever there is trade to be had, with goods most towns have only heard of.\n\nTheir ways began with the crew of an ore hauler that came down with a dead drive and no way back up. Rather than sell the hull for scrap, its purser, Ines Okoro, sold its cargo, its passage and its debts to whoever would buy, one bargain at a time, until the crew owned a landing pad and a radio and the ships above were calling them. The exchange still keeps the hauler's manifest, every bargain the enclave has struck written in it, and on the night the ledger is read aloud the chair is called the purser.\n\nThey say "noted" where others would say thank you, and they never name a price they will not keep. They are polite, exact and very well armed, and their marshals wear the armour of another world. Each market is run by its pad master, and the enclave by the chair of the exchange.</description>
    <pawnSingular>broker</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>brokers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>chair of the exchange</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Enclave</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_EnclaveTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Enclave</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/EnclaveTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.50, 0.74, 0.82)</li>
      <li>(0.76, 0.92, 0.96)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>17</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.3</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <backstoryFilters Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Offworld</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.6</commonality>
      </li>
      <li>
        <categories>
          <li>Outlander</li>
        </categories>
        <commonality>0.4</commonality>
      </li>
    </backstoryFilters>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.15)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Hussar>
        <Genie MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.05</Genie>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.05</Highmate>
        <Starjack MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.04</Starjack>
        <VRE_Archon MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty,vanillaracesexpanded.archon">0.03</VRE_Archon>
        <DV_Avaloi MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.avaloi">0.03</DV_Avaloi>
        <VREA_AndroidAwakened MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.android">0.03</VREA_AndroidAwakened>
        <AG_Lapis MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.02</AG_Lapis>
        <Askbarn MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Rimsenal.Askbarn">0.02</Askbarn>
        <Uredd MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Rimsenal.Askbarn">0.01</Uredd>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Exchange</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>Everything has a price, and a fair price is the closest thing to justice the stars allow. The body is a tool to be kept sharp and made better, a bargain once struck is kept to the last digit, and the ships above and the towns below are both the enclave's to serve. What a machine can do, a machine should do: Okoro's crew had no hands to spare, and the enclave still has none.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Transhumanist</li>
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Trader</li>
      <!-- No hands to spare since Okoro's crew: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's progressive. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Progressive</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
      <Structure_Ideological MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">3</Structure_Ideological>
      <Structure_Archist MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">1</Structure_Archist>
    </structureMemeWeights>
    <styles>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Techist</li>
    </styles>
    <caravanTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_Enclave_Goods</li>
      <li>Rimfolk_Caravan_Enclave_Exotic</li>
    </caravanTraderKinds>
    <visitorTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Visitor_Enclave</li>
    </visitorTraderKinds>
    <baseTraderKinds Inherit="False">
      <li>Rimfolk_Base_Enclave</li>
    </baseTraderKinds>
    <pawnGroupMakers Inherit="False">
      <li>
        <!-- A fight: the enclave's marshals, and hired guns -->
        <kindDef>Combat</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>10</Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>
          <Mercenary_Gunner>4</Mercenary_Gunner>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>2</Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Peaceful</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>20</Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>
          <Villager_Child MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">3</Villager_Child>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>6</Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>3</Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>
        </options>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- A caravan on the ground: a factor, pack beasts for the crates, marshals; the lander takes the factor and marshals only -->
        <kindDef>Trader</kindDef>
        <traders>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>1</Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>
        </traders>
        <carriers>
          <Muffalo>5</Muffalo>
          <Dromedary>4</Dromedary>
          <Horse>3</Horse>
          <Alpaca>2</Alpaca>
        </carriers>
        <guards>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>10</Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>
          <Mercenary_Gunner>3</Mercenary_Gunner>
        </guards>
      </li>
      <li>
        <kindDef>Settlement</kindDef>
        <options>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>10</Rimfolk_Enclave_Marshal>
          <Mercenary_Gunner>4</Mercenary_Gunner>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>8</Rimfolk_Enclave_Hand>
          <Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>2</Rimfolk_Enclave_Factor>
        </options>
      </li>
    </pawnGroupMakers>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="ColonyCouncil.PeopleExtension">
        <calling>brokers</calling>
        <!-- Their age over the years (Peoples/PeopleAges.cs): already at the height of what anyone knows; it keeps its pad by keeping up, and falls back to the industrial age if cut off. -->
        <agePace>8</agePace>
        <ageLimit>3</ageLimit>
        <townWord>market</townWord>
        <townWords>markets</townWords>
        <head>pad master</head>
        <heir>second pad master</heir>
        <envoy>enclave factor</envoy>
        <trader>factor</trader>
        <courier>runner</courier>
        <couriers>runners</couriers>
        <caravanWeight>0.7</caravanWeight>
        <camps>
          <li>Council_Camp_FarMerchants</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Spacers</li>
          <li>Rimfolk_Camp_Salvagers</li>
          <li>Council_Camp_Market</li>
        </camps>
        <plan>Rimfolk_Plan_LandingMarket</plan>
        <honours>the kept bargain, the exact figure and the body made better</honours>
        <fears>the default, the debt nobody pays and being stranded</fears>
        <sayings>
          <li>A bargain struck is kept to the last digit.</li>
          <li>Everything has a price, and a fair one exists.</li>
          <li>Nobody is stranded who has something to sell.</li>
          <li>Terms first, then talk.</li>
        </sayings>
        <townGoods>
          <ComponentIndustrial>8~16</ComponentIndustrial>
          <ComponentSpacer>1~3</ComponentSpacer>
          <Plasteel>40~100</Plasteel>
          <MedicineIndustrial>6~12</MedicineIndustrial>
          <Chocolate>20~40</Chocolate>
          <Silver>300~700</Silver>
        </townGoods>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md "Their gear, their kinds of people and their gifts"): the enclave's hands,
    factors and chair vary freely around their signature, a coat dyed pale cyan of whatever cut, over the game's and Vanilla
    Apparel Expanded's industrial clothes and Rimsenal's spacer unisuits, with data glasses (Rimsenal), tool belts, medic
    bags and packs (Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories, never its soldiers' belts), the factor's ruffled shirt and
    Royalty's finery, the chair's psychic finery (Royalty, Vanilla Psycasts Expanded's eltex). The marshals are its soldiers
    and wear one issue: recon armour and its helmet over Rimsenal's spacer bodysuit (a collar shirt without it), a charge
    weapon (the game's, Vanilla Weapons Expanded's charge guns, its coilguns' gauss rifles, Rimsenal's and Advanced
    Armaments' charge guns, Rimsenal's smart rifles), a smoke or shield belt (Vanilla Apparel Expanded - Accessories' ranged
    shield belt). Hands carry components, chemfuel or medicine. A few have a psylink (Royalty; with Vanilla Psycasts
    Expanded a harmonist's, empath's, skipmaster's, protector's or warlord's path), a few are A RimWorld of Magic's
    technomancers or psionics, and a few had a gene put in (Biotech: strong immunity, fast healing, good looks; Alpha Genes'
    long life for the chair). Without any mod: jackets, dusters and flak, the game's industrial clothes, recon armour,
    charge rifles and lances.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_EnclaveKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Enclave</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.08</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <invFoodDef>MealSurvivalPack</invFoodDef>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- Pale cyan on the marshals' armour, as the enclave issues it. -->
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_ArmorRecon</apparelDef><color>(0.66, 0.84, 0.90)</color></li>
      <li><apparelDef>Apparel_ArmorHelmetRecon</apparelDef><color>(0.66, 0.84, 0.90)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
    <techHediffsMoney>200~1200</techHediffsMoney>
    <techHediffsTags>
      <li>Simple</li>
      <li>Advanced</li>
    </techHediffsTags>
    <techHediffsChance>0.15</techHediffsChance>
  </PawnKindDef>

